# Line-ending policy.
#
# Goal: what GitHub Actions checks out must be byte-for-byte identical to the
# blobs this repository stores, so the zips attached to a release match the
# tagged source exactly.
#
# What went wrong without this file: the repository stores LF, but the Windows
# runners default to core.autocrlf=true, which converts every LF to CRLF on
# checkout. The v0.1.0 zip therefore shipped ofd_renderer.h at 15,650 bytes
# (CRLF, 401 lines) while the repository stores 15,249 bytes (LF).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts must stay CRLF: they rely on ^ line continuation and
# parenthesised blocks, and a bare-LF script can break on some hosts.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary deliverables and fixtures
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
